• DESK PLACEMENT: Position desks 1.5-2.5m from walls, NEVER in room center. Create distinct workstation zones. If multiple desks, separate them by at least 2.5m.
• CHAIR POSITIONING: Place chair directly in front of desk (0.5-1.0m away), facing toward desk. Chair and desk form a single functional unit.
• BOOKSHELVES - CRITICAL: Bookshelves MUST be positioned near walls (within 0.5m of east/west/north/south wall). NEVER place bookshelves in the center of the room.
  - Recommended positions: Near corners or along long walls
  - Face bookshelves into room (shelves accessible, not facing walls)
• TRAFFIC FLOW: Keep center 40% of room completely clear for movement. Create natural pathways between workstations.
• FUNCTIONAL ZONES: Group desk+chair+monitor as workstation units. Position bookshelves as perimeter storage, not obstacles.
• REALISTIC OFFICE: Think "real office layout" - desks create workspaces, bookshelves line walls, center stays open.
